let jumpT = 0, shocks: never[] = [];       // owner: both stay at rest — the leap was removed
// owner: impacto() removed — only the strike is left.
// ============================================================
// THE WORLD ANSWERS BACK
// Monsters used to spawn, stop and stand there: scenery with hit points. Now they walk
// in, and one that reaches you blocks part of the work until it is dealt with. Beating
// one leaves something on the ground that has to be *picked up by hand* — a tap on the
// world itself, not on the big button. And every couple of minutes the neighbourhood
// calls: show up inside the window and the whole street works with you for a while.
//
// Deliberate rule for all of it: nothing here heals tiredness and nothing here changes
// how tiredness is made. Tapping away the team's exhaustion is exactly what erased the
// GO FAST / GO STEADY decision once before (see NOTES). Every reward below is a
// multiplier on output or a lump of impact, both of which are still multiplied by team
// health — so a worn-out team gets less out of the world too.
// ============================================================
let drops: Drop[] = [], mutiraoT = 0, chamada = null, chamadaT = 0, mobChao = 0;
let chamadaDobrada = false, diaNovo = false, voltouDepoisDe = 0;

// ============================================================
// THE SUPER — three combos land, and the next swing is not a swing
//
// What it pays in, and why it is not a bigger hit. NOTES has the ceiling written down:
// taps are 4–7% of total impact, so doubling or tripling a swing could never feel worth a
// build-up. So the super pays in the two currencies the world layer already uses:
//   1. the road — every trouble on it goes down at once, each leaving what it was holding,
//      which is worth up to the −30% they were taking off production;
//   2. a short window where the street works with you, ×superMult for superSeg seconds,
//      applied exactly where the mutirão is applied.
// What gates it is NOT the combo count — nine swings is 1.3s while holding. It is
// `superRecarga`: after it fires, combos stop counting for 22s. That makes the super a
// once-every-~23s event whether you are holding the button or poking at it, which is what
// lets the payoff be tuned as a per-23s thing.
//
// The rule the whole file obeys: **it does not touch tiredness, in either direction.**
// Not the emission, not the decay, not a heal. The one shape this game has already died
// of is automation that pays down tiredness.
//
// FOR THE ESTÉTICA AGENT — everything the spectacle needs is here and readable:
//   superFx      · null, or { t, dur, sx } while the effect plays. t counts up in seconds.
//   superT       · seconds of window left (0 when it is over)
//   superCarga   · 0..CFG.superCombos, how charged it is
//   superCd      · seconds until it can start charging again
//   superPronto()· true while it is armed and the next swing will fire it
//   #flash.super · the full-frame wash class, fired by piscarSuper()
// desenharSuper() below is a placeholder screen effect and is meant to be replaced.
// ============================================================

// One player swing's worth of charge. Only the player's own swings count: the neighbours'
