// on a table never builds a super. Same reasoning as AUTO-FIRE's focus.
// owner: carregarSuper() removed — only the strike is left.
// owner: piscarSuper() removed — only the strike is left.
// owner: dispararSuper() removed — only the strike is left.
// owner: atualizarSuper() removed — only the strike is left.

// ============================================================
// SKILLS — a category apart, and AUTO-FIRE is its first entry
//
// Why this is not a second "Neighbors join in": U4 is a flat 2 taps/s that runs whether or
// not anything is happening, forever, for free. AUTO-FIRE produces nothing by itself. It
// burns FOCUS, and focus is only earned by showing up for the world — clearing a trouble,
// picking a drop up off the ground, answering the kitchen. Its fuel is the world layer,
// which is rate-capped by design (one arrival per 7s, three alive at most), so the skill
// cannot become an income engine no matter how long it is left alone. Put the phone down
// and the wand goes quiet, which is the exact opposite of the failure this game already
// survived once.
//
// It also never touches tiredness: its shots pass `auto`, which suppresses U2's heal.
// ============================================================
// owner: ganharFoco() removed with the AUTO-FIRE skill.
// owner: armarWand() removed with the AUTO-FIRE skill.
// while it is channelling the wand shoots on its own, through the same swing the player
