// 93 75 77 65 72 against the street's 141 101 83 60 66, and left->right 87 92 80 64 58
// against 63 86 115 125 61. Three things fall out of those numbers and they are the whole
// brief: the square is DARKER at the top than the street is (one enormous canopy over it
// instead of an open slot of sky — 12% of its top fifth is sky against the street panel's
// 35%), its chroma CLIMBS toward the ground (16.6 -> 24.3 by fifths, warm earth and fruit),
// and it is lit from the LEFT with the tree mass on the right, where the street is a
// symmetric corridor. Same neighbourhood, same palette families, same light, same hero.
